Usage:
  mdev test [PHPUnit arguments...]
  mdev test static [PHPUnit arguments...]
  mdev test unit [PHPUnit options...]
  mdev test integration [PHPUnit options...]
  mdev test fast [--dry-run]

Runs PHPUnit in the running app container using its configured PHP runtime.
The plain form passes arguments directly to vendor/bin/phpunit.

The static, unit, and integration helpers compare the Commerce checkout to
MDEV_TEST_BASE (default: origin/2.4-develop, with local fallbacks), and include
staged, unstaged, and untracked files. Set MDEV_TEST_BASE to compare against a
different branch or commit.

  static       Runs the Magento PHP LiveCodeTest class with a temporary
               changed-file list, including the current branch diff.
  unit         Runs changed unit test files and conventional tests related to
               changed source files.
  integration  Runs changed integration test files and conventional tests
               related to changed source files.

Unit and integration helpers accept PHPUnit options such as --filter. Pass a
test file or directory to run it explicitly. If no related test target can be
found, the helper exits with an error instead of running the entire suite.
Xdebug is not forced; use the app-xdebug service separately when coverage is
required.

Fast mode runs changed-file static checks and focused unit tests in parallel,
then related integration and integrity tests against an isolated RAM-backed
MariaDB and reusable Docker-volume sandbox. Integrity checks cover DI and
changed block/template/configuration types. DI checks validate changed-module
files and retain all native global merges. Block instantiation scans only
modules with block changes, using Magento's native assertions.
Service-contract implementations,
Api/ contracts and ResourceModel/ changes select related REST tests. Resolver
and GraphQL schema changes select related GraphQL tests. Changed API tests are
always included. Unmapped coverage is reported, not silently expanded to the
entire suite. This is focused feedback, not full regression or JavaScript coverage.

Choose a feature base with MDEV_TEST_BASE. Fast mode has a 300-second budget
(MDEV_TEST_TIMEOUT overrides it) and fails on timeout or any failing suite.
MDEV_TEST_REBUILD=1 forces a fresh isolated integration installation.
Logs, timings, and the local test DB password are kept in .docker/tests/.
Only one fast run is allowed at a time. Fixture module deployment and generated
code are isolated in the test-app container, not written to your checkout.
API requests use its private HTTP server and disposable test database; a DB
snapshot is restored after every API suite, including failures.
--dry-run is also supported as the first option of static/unit/integration.

Examples:
  mdev test static
  mdev test unit --filter testConstructorIntegrity
  mdev test integration --filter testSomething
  mdev test unit /magento/app/code/Magento/Catalog/Test/Unit
  MDEV_TEST_BASE=HEAD^ mdev test fast --dry-run
  MDEV_TEST_BASE=HEAD^ mdev test fast

The misspelled alias "intgration" is also accepted.
